<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H5
/P 229 0 R
/T (Then, in August 2025, after more than 18 months of research, testing, and technical design, we launched our first placemaking event in the Tenderloin, paying a professional Improver and thanking volunteers with SFLuv tokens that they then spent together at our newest merchant. Today, we are proud to celebrate SFLuv's inaugural year of operations with the publication of our first Annual Report.)
/E (Then, in August 2025, after more than 18 months of research, testing, and technical design, we launched our first placemaking event in the Tenderloin, paying a professional Improver and thanking volunteers with SFLuv tokens that they then spent together at our newest merchant. Today, we are proud to celebrate SFLuv's inaugural year of operations with the publication of our first Annual Report.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
290 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H5
/P 229 0 R
/T (As you read this report, we hope you come to appreciate what we have come to treasure most: the deep and real relationships being built among our community partners, including the Tenderloin Merchants Association and Tenderloin Community Benefit District; our affiliate partners, including St. Anthony Foundation, Glide, and City Hope. We are equally inspired by the new relationships forming among volunteers, and between volunteers and Tenderloin merchants. This joyful and unanticipated consequence of pursuing economic development through community engagement feels, to us, a little magical.)
/E (As you read this report, we hope you come to appreciate what we have come to treasure most: the deep and real relationships being built among our community partners, including the Tenderloin Merchants Association and Tenderloin Community Benefit District; our affiliate partners, including St. Anthony Foundation, Glide, and City Hope. We are equally inspired by the new relationships forming among volunteers, and between volunteers and Tenderloin merchants. This joyful and unanticipated consequence of pursuing economic development through community engagement feels, to us, a little magical.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
291 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H5
/P 229 0 R
/T (We are also tremendously proud of the technological progress we have made this year and deeply grateful to our generous donors. They have allowed us the privilege of serving the community without the external pressures that a for-profit tech company can feel to go faster and grow bigger for the sake of getting bigger and faster. We are free to do what makes sense for the stability and health of the community we serve. In turn, the community has been patient with us, offering feedback, showing genuine interest, and celebrating each new feature and improvement. We are so thankful to all who are using our software and who have helped us get better.)
/E (We are also tremendously proud of the technological progress we have made this year and deeply grateful to our generous donors. They have allowed us the privilege of serving the community without the external pressures that a for-profit tech company can feel to go faster and grow bigger for the sake of getting bigger and faster. We are free to do what makes sense for the stability and health of the community we serve. In turn, the community has been patient with us, offering feedback, showing genuine interest, and celebrating each new feature and improvement. We are so thankful to all who are using our software and who have helped us get better.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
